# Cursor Project Rules for V2VBot

## Editing Conventions
- Do not reformat unrelated code. Preserve existing indentation and style.
- Use small, focused edits; one concern per change.
- Add imports and dependencies explicitly when needed.
- For existing code references in replies, use code references with start:end:filepath per project docs.
- For new code proposals in replies, use fenced markdown with a language tag.

## Architecture & Performance
- Keep audio at 16 kHz mono end-to-end; Opus 20 ms frames.
- Maintain streaming pipelines: STT partials, LLM partials, TTS chunked output.
- Ensure barge-in support: mic VAD cancels TTS and LLM quickly.
- Avoid per-frame allocations; reuse buffers; pre-warm models.

## Python Backend
- Framework: FastAPI + aiortc + asyncio; prefer uvloop.
- Structure: follow `docs/folder-structure.md`.
- Typing for public APIs; meaningful variable names.

## Frontend
- Minimal UI with WebRTC media and a DataChannel; avoid heavy frameworks.
- Respect constraints in `docs/architecture-rules.md`.

## Docs Discipline
- If an edit changes architecture/behavior materially, update `docs/` in the same PR.

## Security & Secrets
- Do not hardcode secrets; use environment variables.
- Keep logs free of PII; redact transcripts if persisted.

